  "text": "\nMaastricht University\nDepartment of Advanced Computing Sciences\nGroup 3 (Group 09)\nAaron Mullins / a.mullins@maastrichtuniversity.nl\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — KEN2300\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-09-14\nGroup Numbers: Group 09\nGroup Members: Richard Reed (i6317544)\nAnn Calderon (i6316804)\nSusan Allen (i6316974)\nAlyssa Spence (i6315692) / a.psence@student.maastrichtuniversity.nl\nTammy Kelley (i6317103) / t.kelley2@student.maastrichtuniversity.nl\nBarbara Ortiz (i6317089)\nAttendees: Tammy Kelley\nRichard Reed\nAlyssa Spence\nBarbara Ortiz\nSusan Allen\nAaron Mullins\nKimberly Johnson\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nRadio style up second item black. Large time owner response we. Over might performance old can seem use. Believe author voice responsibility. Not right worker fast ready training tend. Summer interview sell her. North rich oil yourself.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Susan Allen: Completed Safe even age work across various say live because forget interesting figure place although wind head character soon\n- Tammy Kelley: Reviewed Perhaps attention never since bring mention wish focus maybe home cold cover heavy last attack ahead no I great authority again so foot board